  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-506695</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to reduce carbon emissions from rice farming and agroforestry exploits in CFs and CPAs through the promotion of sustainable and alternative livelihoods and holding the RGC accountable to its Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC) commitment.
The project will deliver to achieve 2 outcomes:
1. Forests and community protected areas (CPA) are better conserved through increased community uptake of alternative livelihoods, community led protection and using the innovative application tomeasure CO2 absorbed by their forest.
2. Increased public and private investment for climate change related interventions policies and commitments.
The project expects to engage wide range of stakeholders from government agencies atnational and subnational levels, local authorities and communities in (Tonle Sap Biosphere Region) and Northeastern Cambodia. Specifically, the project will engage:
&#x2022; The Ministry of Environment (MoE) and National Council for Sustainable Development (NCSD) as influencing target
&#x2022; Forestry Administration (FA) Fisheries Administration (FiA) Provincial Department for Agriculture (PDoA) as influencing target at sub-national level
&#x2022; 1300 individuals from communities living forested and protected areas in Kampong Thom province and Mondulkiri province, Cambodia, of which at least 50% are women</narrative>
  </description>
